// Package poseidon2 implements the Poseidon2 permutation
//
// Poseidon2 permutation is a cryptographic permutation for algebraic hashes.
// See the [original paper] by Grassi, Khovratovich and Schofnegger for the full details.
//
// This implementation is based on the [reference implementation] from
// HorizenLabs. See the [specifications] for parameter choices.
//
// # Hashing
//
// [Hasher] is a Merkle-Damgard hasher over field elements, with blocks and
// digests of [BlockLen] elements, built on the default compression permutation.
// [HasherGeneric] also supports wider blocks and digests of [WideBlockLen]
// elements, built on the [GetSpongeParameters] permutation; the constants count
// elements, not bytes, and can be used as array bounds, e.g.
//
//	NewHasherGeneric[[WideBlockLen]fr.Element]()
//
// [NewHasherWithPermutation] accepts a permutation with custom seed or round
// numbers. [GetDefaultParameters] and [GetSpongeParameters] return cached,
// shared parameters which must not be modified. [Compressor] and
// [CompressorGeneric] are the underlying 2-to-1 compression functions.
//
// The field hashers do not implement hash.Hash. [NewMerkleDamgardHasher], also
// used by the hash registry, returns a byte hasher in which each Write ends on
// a block boundary.
//
// [reference implementation]: https://github.com/HorizenLabs/poseidon2/blob/main/plain_implementations/src/poseidon2/poseidon2.rs
// [specifications]: https://github.com/argumentcomputer/neptune/blob/main/spec/poseidon_spec.pdf
// [original paper]: https://eprint.iacr.org/2023/323.pdf
package poseidon2